		,Industrial Fuel]
	~	g pollutant
	~		|

BAU Industrial Energy Use by Fuel Type and Process[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel
,Industrial Process] :EXCEPT:                  [Industry Category,electricity if,Industrial Process\
		], [cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239,Industrial Fuel,industrial process end use\
		]=
	ZIDZ(
	  SUM(
	    BAU Output from Industrial Equipment Installed During Model Run[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Process,Model Run Vintage
	!]
	    * BAU Last Year Industrial Equipment Fuel Type Shares in Electricity Equivalent by Vintage\
		[Industry Category,Industrial Process
	,Industrial Fuel,Model Run Vintage!]
	    * BAU Last Year Energy Intensity of Industrial Production in Electricity Equivalent by Vintage\
		[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process,Model Run Vintage!]
	  )

	  + BAU Output from New Industrial Equipment[Industry Category,Industrial Process]
	  * BAU Share of New Industrial Equipment Allocated by Fuel Type in Electricity Equivalent\
		[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel
	,Industrial Process]
	  * BAU Energy Intensity of Industrial Production by Fuel and Process for New Equipment in Electricity Equivalent\
		[Industry Category
	,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process]
	
	  + BAU Output from Preexisting Industrial Equipment[Industry Category,Industrial Process\
		]
	  * Start Year BAU Fuel Type Shares in Electricity Equivalent[Industry Category,Industrial Process\
		,Industrial Fuel]
	  * Start Year Energy Intensity of Industrial Production in Electricity Equivalent[Industry Category\
		],
	  1 - PIFURfE Percentage Industry Fuel Use Reduction for Electricity[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Process]
	) ~~|
BAU Industrial Energy Use by Fuel Type and Process[Industry Category,electricity if
,Industrial Process] :EXCEPT: [cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239,electricity if\
		,industrial process end use]=
	SUM(
	  BAU Output from Industrial Equipment Installed During Model Run[Industry Category,\
		Industrial Process,Model Run Vintage
	!]
	  * BAU Last Year Industrial Equipment Fuel Type Shares in Electricity Equivalent by Vintage\
		[Industry Category,Industrial Process
	,electricity if,Model Run Vintage!]
	  * BAU Last Year Energy Intensity of Industrial Production in Electricity Equivalent by Vintage\
		[Industry Category,electricity if,Industrial Process,Model Run Vintage!]
	)

	+ BAU Output from New Industrial Equipment[Industry Category,Industrial Process]
	* BAU Share of New Industrial Equipment Allocated by Fuel Type in Electricity Equivalent\
		[Industry Category,electricity if
	,Industrial Process]
	* BAU Energy Intensity of Industrial Production by Fuel and Process for New Equipment in Electricity Equivalent\
		[Industry Category,electricity if,Industrial Process
	]
	
	+ BAU Output from Preexisting Industrial Equipment[Industry Category,Industrial Process\
		]
	* Start Year BAU Fuel Type Shares in Electricity Equivalent[Industry Category,Industrial Process\
		,electricity if]
	* Start Year Energy Intensity of Industrial Production in Electricity Equivalent[Industry Category\
		] ~~|
BAU Industrial Energy Use by Fuel Type and Process[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Industrial Fuel,industrial process end use]=
	BAU Cement Generic Process Energy by Fuel and Process[Industrial Fuel,industrial process end use\
		]
	+ BAU Cement Module Fuel Added to Industry 239 Energy Use by Fuel Type[Industrial Fuel\
		]
	* Cement Energy Use Process Shares[Industrial Fuel,industrial process end use]
	~	BTU
	~	"Industrial Equipment Fuel Type Shares in Electricity Equivalent by \
		Vintage" add to 1 for each industry category, so that variable is \
		expecting to be multiplied by total output of each industry category.
	|

BAU Industrial Equipment Annual Costs and Annual Financing Repayment per Unit Energy in Electricity Equivalent\
		[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process] :EXCEPT:     [Industry Category\
		,electricity if,Industrial Process]=
	BAU Present Value of Industrial Equipment Costs per Unit Energy[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel\
		,Industrial Process]
	/ (1 - PIFURfE Percentage Industry Fuel Use Reduction for Electricity[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Process])
	* XIDZ(
	    BAU New Industrial Equipment Energy Intensity[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel,\
		Industrial Process],
	    SYIEUEFbIPaF Start Year Industrial Equipment Unit Energy Factor by Industrial Process and Fuel\
		[Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process],
	    1
	  ) ~~|
BAU Industrial Equipment Annual Costs and Annual Financing Repayment per Unit Energy in Electricity Equivalent\
		[Industry Category,electricity if,Industrial Process]=
	BAU Present Value of Industrial Equipment Costs per Unit Energy[Industry Category,electricity if\
		,Industrial Process]
	* XIDZ(
	    BAU New Industrial Equipment Energy Intensity[Industry Category,electricity if,Industrial Process\
		],
	    SYIEUEFbIPaF Start Year Industrial Equipment Unit Energy Factor by Industrial Process and Fuel\
		[electricity if,Industrial Process],
	    1
	  )
	~	$/BTU
	~	Cost per unit of energy service delivered (electricity equivalent basis): \
		the cost per BTU consumed, times the BTUs consumed per unit of service. \
		The static electricity versus combustion efficiency level comes from \
		PIFURfE (industry specific); the trailing ratio is each fuel's new \
		equipment energy intensity relative to its start year unit energy factor, \
		which equals one in the start year and then tracks BAU efficiency \
		improvement over time by fuel and process, so fuels whose new equipment \
		improves faster become relatively cheaper per unit of service in the fuel \
		choice logit. XIDZ guards fuels with no unit energy factor data by \
		defaulting the ratio to one.
	|

BAU Industrial Equipment Annual Financing Repayment per Unit Energy[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process]=
	BAU Industrial Equipment Capital Cost per Unit Energy After Subsidy[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process]
	* BAU Capital Recovery Factor by Industry Fuel and Process[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel\
		,Industrial Process]
	~	$/BTU
	~		|

BAU Industrial Equipment Capital Cost per Unit Energy After Subsidy[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process] :EXCEPT:   [Industry Category,Industrial Fuel,\
		industrial heating process]=
	BAU Industrial Equipment Capital Cost per Unit Energy Before Subsidy[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process] ~~|
BAU Industrial Equipment Capital Cost per Unit Energy After Subsidy[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,industrial heating process]=
	BAU Industrial Equipment Capital Cost per Unit Energy Before Subsidy[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,industrial heating process]
	- BAU Clean Industrial Heat Investment Subsidy Rate[industrial heating process,Industrial Fuel\
		]
	~	$/BTU
	~		|

BAU Industrial Equipment Capital Cost per Unit Energy Before Subsidy[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process] :EXCEPT:   [Industry Category,Industrial Fuel,\
		other nonprocess]=
	IECCpUAEU Industrial Equipment Capital Cost per Unit Annual Energy Use[Industrial Fuel\
		,Industrial Process] ~~|
BAU Industrial Equipment Capital Cost per Unit Energy Before Subsidy[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,other nonprocess]=
	IECCpUAEU Industrial Equipment Capital Cost per Unit Annual Energy Use[Industrial Fuel\
		,other nonprocess]
	* (1 - PoONEUTiMEbIC Perc of Other Nonprocess Eqpt E Use That is Mobile Eqpt by Indst Category\
		[Industry Category])
	
	+
	
	IECCpUAEU Industrial Eqpt Capital Cost per Unit Annual E Use for Mobile Eqpt[Industrial Fuel\
		]
	* PoONEUTiMEbIC Perc of Other Nonprocess Eqpt E Use That is Mobile Eqpt by Indst Category\
		[Industry Category]
	~	$/BTU
	~		|

BAU Industrial Equipment Energy Use from Input Data by Industrial Process[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process] :EXCEPT: [cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Industrial Fuel,industrial process end use]=
	BAU Industrial Fuel Use for Energy from Input Data before CCS after Adjustments[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel]
	* BAU Percentage Fuel Use by Industrial Process with Fallback Data[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process] ~~|
BAU Industrial Equipment Energy Use from Input Data by Industrial Process[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Industrial Fuel,industrial process end use]=
	BAU Industrial Fuel Use for Energy from Input Data before CCS after Adjustments[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Industrial Fuel]
	* BAU Percentage Fuel Use by Industrial Process with Fallback Data[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Industrial Fuel,industrial process end use]
	* (1 - Cement Carveout Share of Energy by Fuel[Industrial Fuel])
	~	BTU
	~	THE CEMENT RESIDUAL RESTRUCTURE (Phase 3a): scaling 239's process- end-use \
		cells of this data-spine variable by one minus the cement carveout share \
		makes the ENTIRE downstream equipment structure - output apportionment, \
		start-year fuel shares, industry energy intensity, preexisting and vintage \
		stocks, new-equipment purchases, and capex - represent the non-cement \
		residual (lime, gypsum, ceramics) natively. The output-share inflation and \
		industry- intensity deflation cancel exactly, so nonprocess end uses keep \
		full-239 energy and the start-year residual equals (1 - share) x the \
		legacy value per cell. This makes energy conservation under \
		fuel-reallocating levers, thermal-battery service, clean-heat subsidies, \
		and equipment capex all residual-correct by construction (retiring the \
		Phase 1b interim scalings). SYNC NOTE: the first two factors duplicate the \
		main branch - mirror edits.
	|

BAU Industrial Equipment Energy Use from Input Data by Industrial Process in Electricity Equivalent\
		[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process] :EXCEPT:    [Industry Category\
		,electricity if,Industrial Process]=
	BAU Industrial Equipment Energy Use from Input Data by Industrial Process[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process]
	* (1 - PIFURfE Percentage Industry Fuel Use Reduction for Electricity[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Process]) ~~|
BAU Industrial Equipment Energy Use from Input Data by Industrial Process in Electricity Equivalent\
		[Industry Category,electricity if,Industrial Process]=
	BAU Industrial Equipment Energy Use from Input Data by Industrial Process[Industry Category\
		,electricity if,Industrial Process]
	~	BTU
	~		|

BAU Industrial Equipment Fuel Choice Weight[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process\
		]=
	10000
	* Effective Industrial Equipment Shareweights[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process\
		]
	* (
	  MAX(BAU Industrial Equipment Annual Costs and Annual Financing Repayment per Unit Energy in Electricity Equivalent\
		[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process], 1e-07)
	  / MAX(BAU Minimum Eligible Fuel Cost per Unit Energy in Electricity Equivalent[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Process], 1e-07)
	) ^ IELC Industrial Equipment Logit Coefficient
	~	Dmnl
	~	BAU twin of Industrial Equipment Fuel Choice Weight. See that variable for \
		documentation of the relative-cost logit.
	|

BAU Industrial Equipment Utilization Factor[Industry Category,Industrial Process]=
	MIN(
	  1,
	  ZIDZ(
	    BAU Last Year Output by ISIC Code with Fuels Based on Energy Content[Industry Category ISIC Code\
		],
	    SUM(BAU Potential Output from Industrial Equipment Installed During Model Run[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Process,Model Run Vintage!])
	    + BAU Potential Output from Preexisting Industrial Equipment[Industry Category,Industrial Process\
		]
	  )
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

BAU Industrial Feedstock Use after Adjustments[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel] :EXCEPT:\
		    [energy industries within industry category
,Industrial Fuel], [cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239,Industrial Fuel]=
	BIFU BAU Industrial Fuel Use as Feedstock[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel]
	* (1 + Perc Change in Sectoral Energy Use due to Exogenous GDP Adjustment[industry sector\
		]) ~~|
BAU Industrial Feedstock Use after Adjustments[energy industries within industry category\
		,Industrial Fuel]=
	BIFU BAU Industrial Fuel Use as Feedstock[energy industries within industry category\
		,Industrial Fuel]
	* (1 + Last Year BAU Percent Change in Fuel Production from Calculated Fuel Demand[energy industries within industry category\
		]) ~~|
BAU Industrial Feedstock Use after Adjustments[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Industrial Fuel]=
	BAU Cement Residual Feedstock Use[Industrial Fuel]
	+ BAU Cement Module Fuel Added to Industry 239 Feedstock Use by Fuel Type[Industrial Fuel\
		]
	~	BTU
	~	The cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239 branch blends the non-cement \
		residual (lime, gypsum, ceramics - generic data-driven computation scaled \
		by one minus the cement feedstock share) with the cement module's \
		feedstock stream (petcoke riding the heavy or residual fuel oil element). \
		Calibration-neutral at the start year by construction of the carveout \
		shares.
	|

