BFoCDMbNI BAU Fraction of Clinker Demand Met by Net Imports:INTERPOLATE::=
	GET DIRECT DATA(
	   'InputData/indst/_cement/BFoCDMbNI/BFoCDMbNI.csv',
	   ',',
	   '1',
	   'B2'
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Share of the clinker embodied in this region's cement consumption that is \
		supplied by net imports of cement and clinker (clinker basis: imported \
		cement counts at the clinker ratio, exports subtract). Negative for net \
		exporters, so the module produces more clinker than the region consumes \
		there. Only domestically produced clinker uses energy and emits in this \
		model, so the capacity stocks, pathway logit, production, energy, and \
		process CO2 all run on Total Cement Demand x ratio x (1 - this share) - \
		see Domestic Clinker Demand. Held at its BAU value in the policy case (no \
		leakage or import response is modeled). US 2025 = 0.2436, the value that \
		closes the start-year balance on USGS domestic clinker production (69 Mt) \
		given USGS apparent consumption (110 Mt) and the blend ratio.
	|

