CCF Calcination CO2 Factor by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway]=
	GET DIRECT CONSTANTS(
	   'InputData/indst/_cement/CCF/CCF.csv',
	   ',',
	   'B2*'
	)
	~	g CO2/metric ton
	~	Net calcination (process) CO2 released per metric ton of clinker by \
		pathway: the carbonate-decomposition chemistry, net of any capture \
		integral to the pathway. Dry kiln with precalciner and electric kiln \
		510,071 g/t (EPA GHGI calcination factor; electrification changes \
		combustion, not chemistry); dry kiln with CCS 25,504 g/t at 95 percent \
		capture (NETL 2023 cement CCS baseline and US FEED studies; the captured \
		484,567 g/t is priced - capital, O&M, transport and storage, energy and \
		45Q - from the CCS sector's industry-239 inputs, see Cement CCS Captured \
		Process CO2 per Ton of Clinker). The same capture share is applied to the \
		kiln's fuel CO2 (Cement Pathway CO2 Capture Fraction), since the capture \
		unit treats the whole kiln flue gas; alternative chemistry cement 0 \
		(non-carbonate binder).
	|

CCP CO2 Capture Potential by Electricity Source[Electricity Source]=
	GET DIRECT CONSTANTS(
	   'InputData/ccs/CCP/CPPbES.csv',
