Change in Industrial Fuel Use for Non Energy Purposes due to Feedstock Shifting[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel] :EXCEPT: [cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239,Industrial Fuel\
		]=
	Industrial Fuel Use for Non Energy Purposes[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel]
	- Industrial Fuel Use for Non Energy Purposes Before Feedstock Shifting[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel] ~~|
Change in Industrial Fuel Use for Non Energy Purposes due to Feedstock Shifting[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Industrial Fuel]=
	Industrial Fuel Use for Non Energy Purposes[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Industrial Fuel]
	- Industrial Fuel Use for Non Energy Purposes Before Feedstock Shifting[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Industrial Fuel]
	- Cement Module Fuel Added to Industry 239 Feedstock Use by Fuel Type[Industrial Fuel\
		]
	~	BTU
	~	For cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239 the cement module's \
		feedstock (petcoke) enters the non-energy chain DOWNSTREAM of the shifting \
		step, so the post-minus-pre difference must subtract it to measure only \
		genuine shifting of the non-cement residual - otherwise the module's \
		petcoke reads as a 47-TBtu shift and its carbon double-books as process \
		emissions (Phase 2a gate catch, 2026-08-24). The module's feedstock carbon \
		is priced and emitted through Cement Process CO2 Intensity per Ton by \
		Pathway.
	|

Change in Industry Sector Carbon Tax Rebate due to CCS[Industry Category]=
	Industry Sector Carbon Tax Rebate due to CCS[Industry Category]
	- BAU Industry Sector Carbon Tax Rebate due to CCS[Industry Category]
	~	$
	~		|

Change in Industry Sector Carbon Tax Rebate from Output Based Allocation[Industry Category\
		]=
	Industry Sector Carbon Tax Rebate from Output Based Allocation[Industry Category]
	- BAU Industry Sector Carbon Tax Rebate from Output Based Allocation[Industry Category\
		]
	~	$
	~	Policy minus BAU carbon tax handed back under output-based allocation, by \
		industry.
	|

Change in Industry Sector Carbon Tax Rebates[Industry Category]=
	Change in Industry Sector Carbon Tax Rebate due to CCS[Industry Category]
	+ Change in Industry Sector Carbon Tax Rebate from Output Based Allocation[Industry Category\
		]
	~	$
	~	All carbon tax handed back to an industry, policy minus BAU: the rebate on \
		captured combustion CO2 plus output-based allocation. Replaces the \
		CCS-only term in the carbon-tax effects on industry expenditures, the \
		carbon tax rebates total, the industry other-expenditures subtotal and the \
		normalized nonfuel expenditures, so both rebates reach cash flows and \
		passthrough the same way.
	|

