CPAL Cement Pathway Asset Life[Cement Production Pathway]=
	GET DIRECT CONSTANTS(
	   'InputData/indst/_cement/CPAL/CPAL.csv',
	   ',',
	   'B2*'
	)
	~	years
	~	Economic asset life by pathway: the period over which greenfield capital \
		is annualized (capital recovery factor) in the pathway choice cost. \
		Distinct from CPPL campaign length, which sets the overhaul recurrence and \
		the overhaul annualization. Does not drive retirement: capacity built \
		during the run retires through the same campaign-end overhaul-or-replace \
		decisions as the preexisting fleet. US: 30 years for all pathways (NETL \
		2023 cement capital-recovery period; book and techno-economic lives \
		cluster at 20-30 years, physical kiln lives at 35-50+).
	|

CPCaOC New Build Capital Cost per Unit Annual Capacity[Cement Production Pathway]=
	GET DIRECT CONSTANTS(
	   'InputData/indst/_cement/CPCaOC/CPCaOC-new.csv',
	   ',',
	   'B2*'
	)
	~	$/(metric tons/Year)
	~	Greenfield capital cost per metric ton of annual clinker capacity by \
		pathway, kiln only, in 2012 USD. Dry kiln with precalciner 255.21 \
		(ECRA/IEA cost ranges, corroborated by the CemZero reference plant); dry \
		kiln with CCS is the same kiln (255.21), with its capture equipment added \
		from the CCS sector's capital cost in Cement Pathway Capital Cost per Unit \
		Annual Capacity Including Capture Equipment; electric kiln 299.21 (CemZero \
		2018 plasma-kiln plant) and alternative chemistry cement 502.34 (high end \
		of DOE Liftoff 2023 greenfield range).
	|

CPCaOC Overhaul Capital Cost per Unit Annual Capacity[Cement Production Pathway]=
	GET DIRECT CONSTANTS(
	   'InputData/indst/_cement/CPCaOC/CPCaOC-overhaul.csv',
	   ',',
	   'B2*'
	)
	~	$/(metric tons/Year)
	~	Capital cost to overhaul a kiln (shell/drive/controls rebuild) for one \
		more campaign, per metric ton of annual capacity, by pathway, in 2012 USD. \
		US: about 14 percent of the new-build cost, built up from component \
		retrofit costs (ECRA/CSI 2017, ENERGY STAR 2013, EPA 2010 cement NESHAP); \
		read from the same workbook as the new-build cost so the two stay aligned.
	|

CPPL Cement Pathway Campaign Length[Cement Production Pathway]=
	GET DIRECT CONSTANTS(
	   'InputData/indst/_cement/CPPL/CPPL.csv',
	   ',',
	   'B2*'
	)
	~	years
	~	Mean campaign length between kiln overhaul decisions (shell/drive rebuild \
		cycle), by pathway. Used as the mean of the distributed (third-order \
		delay) decision recurrence for both capacity pools and as the \
		annualization period of the overhaul capital recovery factor - distinct \
		from CPAL asset life. US: 25 years, the IEA investment-cycle figure for \
		cement kilns (Levi, Fernandez Pales and Gul, 2020), supported by ECRA/CSI \
		(2017) on rolling equipment replacement after 20-30 years. Because CPPL \
		sets both decision timing and overhaul cost, a sensitivity on it moves \
		both. DELAY3I splits CPPL into three stages of CPPL/3 at TIME STEP 1, so \
		keep sensitivity values above about 9-10 years.
	|

CPRS Cement Preexisting Capacity Overhaul Decision Schedule[Cement Production Pathway\
		]:INTERPOLATE::=
	GET DIRECT DATA(
	   'InputData/indst/_cement/CPRS/CPRS.csv',
	   ',',
	   '1',
	   'B2'
	)
	~	metric tons/Year
	~	Nameplate capacity of the preexisting fleet reaching a kiln \
		overhaul-or-replace decision each year, by pathway. Built from Princeton \
		Net-Zero America fleet age cohorts (pre-2000 cohort at 7 percent per year \
		from 2026; post-2000 cohort reaching 35-year campaign ends over 2036-2045) \
		and spread with a +/-5-year triangular kernel for campaign-timing \
		variation, conserving total capacity. Whether the capacity is overhauled \
		or replaced is decided in the model.
	|

CPSW Cement Pathway Shareweight[Cement Production Pathway]:INTERPOLATE::=
	GET DIRECT DATA(
	   'InputData/indst/_cement/CPSW/CPSW.csv',
	   ',',
	   '1',
	   'B2'
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Entry-gate shareweights by cement production pathway: 0 until a pathway is \
		commercially available and 1 after, so commercialization timing is set in \
		the data. Values between 0 and 1 phase a newly available pathway in. US \
		(judgment from DOE Liftoff readiness, IEA guide, and project status as of \
		2026): dry kiln with precalciner in all years; dry kiln with CCS opens \
		2031, full weight 2033; alternative chemistry cement opens 2034, full \
		2037; electric kiln opens 2035, full 2039.
	|

