CRbQ Capacity Retirements before Quantization[Electricity Source]:=
	GET DIRECT DATA(
	   'InputData/elec/CRbQ/CRbQ.csv',
	   ',',
	   '1',
	   'B2'
	)
	~	MW
	~		|

CRBWvT Cement Replacement Blend Weight vs Tightness[average summer day]=
	GET DIRECT LOOKUPS(
	   'InputData/indst/_cement/CRBW/CRBWvT.csv',
	   ',',
	   '1',
	   'B2'
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Replacement blend weight (the greenfield share of the retire-alternative \
		cost) vs fleet tightness tau. Normalized-logit (Hill) form w = tau^p / \
		(tau^p + k*(1-tau)^p): w(0)=0 in a slack market, w(1)=1 in a tight market; \
		p = steepness (2, judgment); k shifts the midpoint and is solved per \
		region so w at the start-year tightness reproduces the calibrated \
		overhaul-or-replace mix. The subscript element (average summer day) is a \
		placeholder unrelated to the curve, used because SDEverywhere cannot \
		handle unsubscripted lookups; the curve is the same for every pathway.
	|

CRDT CCS Retrofit Deployment Time[Industry Category,Emissions Type]=
	GET DIRECT CONSTANTS(
	   'InputData/ccs/CRDT/CRDT.csv',
	   ',',
	   'B2'
	)
	~	years
	~		|

CRSW Cement Overhaul Shareweight[Cement Production Pathway]:INTERPOLATE::=
	GET DIRECT DATA(
	   'InputData/indst/_cement/CRSW/CRSW.csv',
	   ',',
	   '1',
	   'B2'
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Calibration weight on the overhaul branch of the overhaul-vs-replace \
		choice, capturing stickiness not in the cost comparison (site integration, \
		quarry co-location, permitting). US: 0.097704 for all pathways and years, \
		calibrated so the BAU average overhaul share of dry-kiln capacity reaching \
		a decision over 2026-2050 is 0.485 (a mean retirement age of about 49 \
		years at a 25-year campaign, consistent with the 36-year average fleet age \
		in Princeton Net-Zero America Annex K). Re-solve if the CPCaOC capital \
		costs, CPPL, or IELC change.
	|

CSBS Cement Share of Start Year Capacity Below Standard[Cement Production Pathway]=
	GET DIRECT CONSTANTS(
	   'InputData/indst/_cement/CSBS/CSBS.csv',
	   ',',
	   'B2*'
	)
	~	Dmnl [0,1]
	~	Share of the start-year clinker capacity on each pathway whose kilns fall \
		below a modern energy-performance standard (older wet, long-dry and \
		preheater-only kilns for the US), the pool the kiln performance standard \
		lever can force to an early overhaul-or-retire decision. See the About tab \
		of the workbook in its folder.
	|

CSCC Calcined Clay Plant Capital Cost=
	GET DIRECT CONSTANTS(
	   'InputData/indst/_cement/CSCC/CSCC.csv',
	   ',',
	   'B2'
	)
	~	$/(metric tons/Year)
	~	Capital cost of a calcined clay plant (calciner, dryer, cooler and \
		storage) per tonne of annual calcined-clay capacity, 2012 USD. US value \
		about 110 (about 150 in 2024 dollars): the middle of calcined clay plants \
		built or announced since 2020. See the About tab of the workbook in its \
		folder.
	|

CSCC Calcined Clay Share of Clinker Substitution=
	GET DIRECT CONSTANTS(
	   'InputData/indst/_cement/CSCC/CSCC.csv',
	   ',',
	   'B3'
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Share of the material replacing clinker under policy-driven substitution \
		that is calcined clay (the rest is limestone, fly ash, slag and natural \
		pozzolan, which need no new kilns). US 0.5, the same marginal mix as SCMEI.
	|

