CSoIO Cement Share of Industry 239 Output=
	GET DIRECT CONSTANTS(
	   'InputData/indst/_cement/CSoIO/CSoIO.csv',
	   ',',
	   'B2'
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Cement's share of industry 239's (cement and other nonmetallic minerals) \
		total output by value - used to scale the cement-content-of-concrete \
		lever's tonnage cut into a reduction in buyers' requirements for 239 \
		product in the IO dollar chain (the lever cuts cement purchases only; \
		lime, glass wool, concrete products, and ceramics sales are untouched). US \
		0.1159: USGS 2023 cement value of shipments, deflated to 2012 USD with the \
		CPI-U, over the model's BAU 2025 output for ISIC 239 (2012 USD). Distinct \
		from the module's physical carve-out shares (energy, process CO2), which \
		are computed INITIALs.
	|

CSPAbY Clinker Substitution Potential Available by Year:INTERPOLATE::=
	GET DIRECT DATA(
	   'InputData/indst/_cement/CSPAbY/CSPAbY.csv',
	   ',',
	   '1',
	   'B2'
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Share of the long-run clinker substitution potential (the gap between the \
		BAU clinker ratio and MACtCR) that supplementary cementitious material \
		supply can support in each year: 0 through 2025, 0.4 in 2030, 0.7 in 2040, \
		1.0 in 2050 (EI judgment based on the build-out of calcined clay supply \
		and harvested fly ash; for the US this caps the reachable ratio at about \
		0.75 in 2030 and 0.70 in 2040). Caps the clinker-substitution lever so an \
		early full-deployment schedule cannot outrun SCM supply.
	|

