Fraction New Components by Quality Level[Non Data Center Buildings,Building Component\
		,Building Component Quality]=
	IF THEN ELSE(
	  Boolean Rebate Program for Efficient Components This Year[Building Component] <> 0\
		,
	
	  BFoCSbQL BAU Fraction of Components Sold by Quality Level[Non Data Center Buildings\
		,Building Component,Building Component Quality]
	  * (1 + MSCdtRPbQL Market Share Changes due to Rebate Program by Quality Level[Building Component Quality\
		]),
	
	  BFoCSbQL BAU Fraction of Components Sold by Quality Level[Non Data Center Buildings\
		,Building Component,Building Component Quality]
	) ~~|
Fraction New Components by Quality Level[data centers,Building Component,Building Component Quality\
		]=
	BFoCSbQL BAU Fraction of Components Sold by Quality Level[data centers,Building Component\
		,Building Component Quality]
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Fraction of Additional Clinker Substitution This Year=
	MIN(
	  MAX(MAX(Fraction of Cement Measures Achieved This Year, Intensity Standard Clinker Substitution Fraction\
		),
	      Procurement Clinker Substitution Fraction),
	  CSPAbY Clinker Substitution Potential Available by Year
	)
	* MAX(
	  0,
	  BCtCR BAU Clinker to Cement Ratio
	  - MACtCR Minimum Achievable Clinker to Cement Ratio
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Policy-driven reduction of the clinker-to-cement ratio below its BAU \
		trajectory this year: the gap between the BAU ratio and the minimum \
		achievable ratio MACtCR, times the larger of the cement-measures lever (on \
		the indst cement measures implementation schedule) and the substitution \
		the cement intensity standard calls for, capped by the share of that gap \
		SCM supply can support this year (CSPAbY). At full implementation and full \
		supply the ratio reaches MACtCR.
	|

Fraction of Additional Demand Response Potential Achieved=
	0
	~	Dmnl [0,1]
	~		|

