Fraction of Below Standard Clinker Capacity Forced to Decide Each Year=
	0
	~	Dmnl [0,1,0.01]
	~	Policy lever (cement kiln performance standard): the share of the \
		start-year kiln capacity that falls below an energy-performance standard \
		(CSBS) that is forced each year to face its overhaul-or-retire decision \
		early, at full implementation. Represents retrofit-or-exit rules such as \
		China's clinker energy benchmark and baseline levels (below-baseline kilns \
		had to upgrade or close by end-2025) and India's PAT intensity targets. \
		Forced kilns go through the same overhaul-versus-replace comparison as \
		kilns reaching the end of a campaign; the companion lever Percent \
		Improvement in Overhauled Kiln Energy Intensity sets how much an overhaul \
		improves them. Rides the indst cement kiln standard implementation \
		schedule.
	|

Fraction of Below Standard Clinker Capacity Forced to Decide Each Year This Year=
	Fraction of Below Standard Clinker Capacity Forced to Decide Each Year
	* Selected Policy Implementation Schedule[indst cement kiln standard X]
	~	Dmnl
	~	The cement kiln performance standard lever as implemented this year.
	|

Fraction of Buildable Capacity Actually Built[Electricity Source]=
	XIDZ(
	  New and Retrofit Generation Capacity[Electricity Source],
	
	  Max Capacity Buildable This Year[Electricity Source],
	
	  1
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~		~	:SUPPLEMENTARY 
	|

Fraction of Buildings Owned by Entity after Allocation to Energy Supplier Entities[Cash Flow Entity\
		,Building Type] :EXCEPT:   [nonenergy industries,commercial],[energy supplier cash flow entity\
		,commercial]=
	FoBObE Fraction of Buildings Owned by Entity[Cash Flow Entity,Building Type] ~~|
Fraction of Buildings Owned by Entity after Allocation to Energy Supplier Entities[nonenergy industries\
		,commercial]=
	FoBObE Fraction of Buildings Owned by Entity[nonenergy industries,commercial]
	* (1 - SUM(Share of Output by Energy Supplier Cash Flow Entity[energy supplier cash flow entity\
		!])) ~~|
Fraction of Buildings Owned by Entity after Allocation to Energy Supplier Entities[energy supplier cash flow entity\
		,commercial]=
	FoBObE Fraction of Buildings Owned by Entity[nonenergy industries,commercial]
	* Share of Output by Energy Supplier Cash Flow Entity[energy supplier cash flow entity\
		]
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Fraction of Cement Carbon Price Rebated by Output Based Allocation=
	0
	~	Dmnl [0,1,0.01]
	~	Policy lever (cement output-based allocation): the share of the cement \
		industry's carbon-price liability that is handed back in proportion to \
		clinker output against a benchmark intensity, at full implementation, on \
		top of any allocation already in place (BCAF). This is how every cement \
		emissions trading system (EU ETS, California, Korea, Canada's output-based \
		standard, China's intensity-based allocation) treats the sector: producers \
		keep paying the full price on each marginal tonne, so the pathway choice \
		still sees the whole carbon price, but the average cost they pass on to \
		buyers is only the price on emissions above the benchmark. The rebate is \
		government to industry 239 and lowers the carbon-tax cost passed through \
		to cement buyers. Rides the indst cement carbon price allocation \
		implementation schedule.
	|

Fraction of Cement Carbon Price Rebated by Output Based Allocation This Year=
	Fraction of Cement Carbon Price Rebated by Output Based Allocation
	* Selected Policy Implementation Schedule[indst cement carbon price allocation X]
	~	Dmnl
	~	The cement output-based allocation lever as implemented this year.
	|

Fraction of Cement Demand Purchased under Low Carbon Procurement=
	0
	~	Dmnl [0,1,0.01]
	~	Policy lever (low-carbon cement procurement): the share of this year's \
		cement demand that committed buyers purchase as low-carbon cement, at full \
		implementation. Covers Buy Clean rules for public construction (public \
		works take about half of US cement, so a rule covering all public \
		purchases is roughly 0.5) and private advance market commitments (First \
		Movers Coalition members pledge 10 percent of their purchases by 2030). \
		Low-carbon means cement at or below the LCPT share of last year's fleet \
		average CO2 intensity. The committed volume is served first by existing \
		low-carbon kilns; any shortfall is built as new low-carbon capacity ahead \
		of the cost-driven choice, and the buyers pay the cost premium over \
		conventional cement, split between government and private buyers by the \
		Share of Low Carbon Cement Premium Paid by Government setting. Rides the \
		indst cement procurement implementation schedule.
	|

Fraction of Cement Demand Purchased under Low Carbon Procurement This Year=
	Fraction of Cement Demand Purchased under Low Carbon Procurement
	* Selected Policy Implementation Schedule[indst cement procurement X]
	~	Dmnl
	~	The low-carbon procurement lever as implemented this year.
	|

Fraction of Cement Measures Achieved=
	0
	~	Dmnl [0,1,0.05]
	~	Policy lever (clinker substitution): the share of the long-run clinker \
		substitution potential achieved at full implementation. Covers \
		supplementary cementitious materials (calcined clay, slag, fly ash, \
		natural pozzolans, extra limestone) replacing clinker wherever they are \
		blended - in the cement at the cement plant or added at the concrete plant \
		- since the clinker saved per unit of binder is the same. The potential is \
		the gap between the BAU clinker-to-cement ratio (BCtCR) and the minimum \
		achievable ratio (MACtCR); how fast it can be reached is capped by SCM \
		supply (CSPAbY). Mix optimization that reduces binder per cubic meter \
		belongs to Percent Reduction in Cement Content of Concrete, not here. \
		Rides the indst cement measures implementation schedule.
	|

Fraction of Cement Measures Achieved This Year=
	Fraction of Cement Measures Achieved
	* Selected Policy Implementation Schedule[indst cement measures X]
	~	Dmnl
	~	The clinker-substitution lever as implemented this year, on the indst \
		cement measures implementation schedule.
	|

Fraction of Clinker Demand Met by Net Imports=
	MIN(1, BFoCDMbNI BAU Fraction of Clinker Demand Met by Net Imports * Cement Import Share Response Factor\
		)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Policy-case share of clinker demand met by net imports: the BAU share \
		scaled by the border fee's import response. Equals the BAU share when no \
		border fee is in force.
	|

