Fraction of Fossil Kiln Energy Shifted=
	0
	~	Dmnl [0,1,0.01]
	~	Policy lever (kiln fuel shift): the share of each fossil kiln fuel (coal, \
		petroleum coke, natural gas, diesel) that is shifted to other fuels at \
		full implementation. Where the shifted energy goes is data: CKFSR gives, \
		for each source fuel, the fraction of its shifted energy that goes to \
		alternative fuels (tire-derived fuel, engineered waste fuels, waste oils \
		and solvents, biomass residues, carried on the biomass element and priced \
		at the biomass price), natural gas or hydrogen. With the US values every \
		fossil fuel goes to alternative fuels, so a thermal substitution target T \
		for a fleet that already burns a share A of alternative fuels maps to (T - \
		A) / (1 - A). Thermal energy per ton of clinker is unchanged by the shift. \
		Only the fuel-burning pathways are affected. Rides the indst cement kiln \
		fuel shift implementation schedule.
	|

Fraction of Fossil Kiln Energy Shifted This Year=
	Fraction of Fossil Kiln Energy Shifted
	* Selected Policy Implementation Schedule[indst cement kiln fuel shift X]
	~	Dmnl
	~	The kiln fuel shift lever as implemented this year, on the indst cement \
		kiln fuel shift implementation schedule.
	|

