Government Contribution to Change in Domestic Output by ISIC Code[ISIC Code]=
	Government Contribution to Change in Global Output by ISIC Code[ISIC Code]
	* Domestic Content Share of Consumption by ISIC Code[ISIC Code]
	~	$
	~		|

Government Contribution to Change in Global Output by ISIC Code[ISIC Code]=
	Government Revenue Change Allocated by Mechanism[regular spending]
	* Percent of Government Expenditures by ISIC Code[ISIC Code]
	~	$
	~		|

Government Cost of Industrial Financing Support=
	Government Interest Spread Payments for Industrial Equipment
	+ Government Credit Guarantee Subsidy Cost for Industrial Equipment
	~	$
	~	Total government cost of delivering the industrial cost of capital lever's \
		rate reduction, per the instrument mix in SoFSbI.  The pure derisking \
		share costs nothing by construction.  Zero unless the lever is active AND \
		a scenario sets a nonzero buydown, green bank, or guarantee share.  Flows \
		to the government entity via Industry Sector Change in Nonenergy \
		Expenditures by Entity and to GRA via its own Govt Cash Flow Type element.
	|

Government Credit Guarantee Subsidy Cost for Industrial Equipment=
	SoFSbI Share of Financing Support by Instrument[credit guarantee]
	* CGSCR Credit Guarantee Subsidy Cost Rate
	* SUM(New Qualifying Financed Industrial Capital Expenditures[Industry Category!])
	~	$
	~	Expected-loss (FCRA budget basis) cost of guaranteeing the credit \
		guarantee share of this year's qualifying financed equipment loan \
		originations.  Booked once at origination, matching federal budget scoring.
	|

Government Expenditures by ISIC Code by Year[ISIC Code]=
	GaHEbIC Government Expenditures by ISIC Code[ISIC Code]
	* (1 + BPCiObIC BAU Percent Change in Output by ISIC Code[ISIC Code])
	~	$
	~	Scaled by the EXOGENOUS percent change in output (BPCiObIC), not the \
		endogenous-revenue-blended measure, so that fuel price movements do not \
		tilt the government respending distribution toward energy ISIC codes with \
		no real activity behind the shift.
	|

Government Financing Support Payments to Lenders=
	Government Cost of Industrial Financing Support
	~	$
	~	Government payments received by the financial sector (ISIC 64T66): the \
		interest spread on buydown and green bank shares (keeping lenders whole \
		for the rate reduction), and the credit guarantee subsidy as expected \
		default-loss compensation.  Booked as ordinary lender revenue and kept IN \
		the input-output chain - these payments replace industry production \
		payments for the same lending service, so the government-transfer \
		exclusion convention at the IO handoff deliberately does not apply.  Equal \
		to Government Cost of Industrial Financing Support in this formulation; \
		kept as a separate variable because a future green bank fund structure \
		splits them (capitalization outlay is not a payment to lenders).
	|

Government Incentives for Process Emissions Policies Paid to Abating Industries[Industry Category\
		,Industry Process Emissions Policy] :EXCEPT:          
[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239
,indst cement measures],[oil and gas extraction 06,indst methane capture],[oil and gas extraction 06\
		,indst methane destruction
],[energy pipelines and gas processing 352T353,indst methane capture],[energy pipelines and gas processing 352T353\
		,indst methane destruction
],[chemicals 20,indst f gas substitution],[chemicals 20,indst f gas destruction],[chemicals 20\
		,indst f gas recovery],[chemicals 20
,indst f gas inspct maint retrofit],[chemicals 20,indst N2O abatement],[coal mining 05\
		,indst methane capture],[coal mining 05
,indst methane destruction],[water and waste 36T39,indst methane capture],[water and waste 36T39\
		,indst methane destruction
],[agriculture and forestry 01T03,indst cropland and rice measures],[agriculture and forestry 01T03\
		,indst livestock measures
],[agriculture and forestry 01T03,indst tillage],[other metals 242,indst f gas inspct maint retrofit\
