	,Industrial Process!])
	~	BTU
	~		|

Industrial Fuel Use for Energy Purposes[Industrial Fuel,Industry Category] :EXCEPT:  \
		[natural gas if,Industry Category]=
	Industrial Fuel Use for Energy before CCS and Methane Capture[Industrial Fuel,Industry Category\
		]
	+ Fuel Used for CCS by Industry Sector[Industrial Fuel,Industry Category] ~~|
Industrial Fuel Use for Energy Purposes[natural gas if,Industry Category]=
	MAX(
	  0,
	
	  Industrial Fuel Use for Energy before CCS and Methane Capture[natural gas if,Industry Category\
		]
	  + Fuel Used for CCS by Industry Sector[natural gas if,Industry Category]
	  - Change in Methane Captured by Industry[Industry Category]
	)
	~	BTU
	~		|

Industrial Fuel Use for Non Energy Purposes[Industry Category,Target Industrial Fuel]\
		 :EXCEPT: [cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239,Target Industrial Fuel]=
	Industrial Fuel Use for Non Energy Purposes Before Feedstock Shifting[Industry Category\
		,Target Industrial Fuel]
	* (1 - Fraction of Feedstock Shifted This Year[Industry Category,Target Industrial Fuel\
		])

	+ SUM(Industrial Fuel Use for Non Energy Purposes Before Feedstock Shifting[Industry Category\
		,Source Industrial Fuel!]
	  * IFSR Industrial Fuel Shifting Ratio[Industry Category,Source Industrial Fuel!]
	  * Fraction of Feedstock Shifted This Year[Industry Category,Source Industrial Fuel\
		!]
	  * IFSRF Industrial Feedstock Shifting Recipient Fuel[Source Industrial Fuel!,Target Industrial Fuel\
		]
	  ) ~~|
Industrial Fuel Use for Non Energy Purposes[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Target Industrial Fuel]=
	Industrial Fuel Use for Non Energy Purposes Before Feedstock Shifting[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Target Industrial Fuel]
	* (1 - Fraction of Feedstock Shifted This Year[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Target Industrial Fuel])

	+ SUM(Industrial Fuel Use for Non Energy Purposes Before Feedstock Shifting[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Source Industrial Fuel!]
	  * IFSR Industrial Fuel Shifting Ratio[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239,Source Industrial Fuel\
		!]
	  * Fraction of Feedstock Shifted This Year[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Source Industrial Fuel!]
	  * IFSRF Industrial Feedstock Shifting Recipient Fuel[Source Industrial Fuel!,Target Industrial Fuel\
		]
	  )

	+ Cement Module Fuel Added to Industry 239 Feedstock Use by Fuel Type[Target Industrial Fuel\
		]
	~	BTU
	~	The cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239 branch applies the \
		feedstock-shifting lever to the non-cement residual only (the \
		before-shifting variable carries only the residual for 239), then adds the \
		cement module's feedstock (petcoke) unshifted - fuel shifting for cement's \
		share is the pathway module's mechanism. SYNC NOTE: the first two terms \
		duplicate the generic branch - mirror edits.
	|

Industrial Fuel Use for Non Energy Purposes Before Feedstock Shifting[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel] :EXCEPT: [cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239,Industrial Fuel\
		]=
	BAU Industrial Feedstock Use after Adjustments[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel]
	* (1 + Percent Change in Production due to Policies[Industry Category]) ~~|
Industrial Fuel Use for Non Energy Purposes Before Feedstock Shifting[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Industrial Fuel]=
	BAU Cement Residual Feedstock Use[Industrial Fuel]
	* (1 + Percent Change in Production due to Policies[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		])
	~	BTU
	~	The cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239 branch carries ONLY the \
		non-cement residual (responding to the policy production change as in the \
		generic branch), so the feedstock-shifting lever downstream acts on the \
		residual alone. The cement module's own feedstock (petcoke) is added after \
		the shifting step - see Industrial Fuel Use for Non Energy Purposes - \
		because fuel shifting for cement's share is the pathway module's \
		mechanism, not the generic lever's (adversarial-review finding, \
		2026-08-24; approved lever dispositions).
	|

