Minimum Clinker Ratio of Blended Low Carbon Cement=
	0.5
	~	Dmnl
	~	Lowest clinker share at which a blended cement is sold for general \
		construction: limestone calcined clay cement (LC3-50) is about 50 percent \
		clinker, 30 percent calcined clay, 15 percent limestone and 5 percent \
		gypsum (LC3 project, lc3.ch). Bounds how far blending alone can take \
		procured cement below the fleet average; a stricter threshold than \
		blending can reach must be met by low-carbon kilns. Entered in Vensim.
	|

Minimum Distributed Solar to Meet Capacity Requirement[Building Type,Electricity Source\
		]=
	MIN(
	  Min Required Rooftop Solar Capacity This Year[Building Type],
	  MDSC Maximum Distributed Solar Capacity[Building Type,Electricity Source]
	)
	~	MW
	~		|

Minimum Eligible Cement Pathway Cost per Ton of Clinker=
	VMIN(
	  Cement Pathway Levelized Cost per Ton of Clinker[Cement Production Pathway!]
	  + IF THEN ELSE(
	      CPSW Cement Pathway Shareweight[Cement Production Pathway!] > 0,
	      0,
	      1e+09
	    )
	)
	~	$/metric ton
	~	Cheapest pathway with a positive shareweight: the reference cost for the \
		relative-cost pathway logit, mirroring Minimum Eligible Fuel Cost per Unit \
		Energy in Electricity Equivalent. The ineligibility adder is large in \
		absolute terms because pathway costs are hundreds of dollars per ton.
	|

Minimum Eligible Fuel Cost per Unit Energy in Electricity Equivalent[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Process]=
	VMIN(
	  Industrial Equipment Annual Costs and Annual Financing Repayment per Unit Energy in Electricity Equivalent\
		[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel!,Industrial Process]
	  + IF THEN ELSE(
	      Effective Industrial Equipment Shareweights[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel!\
		,Industrial Process] > 0,
	      0,
	      1
	    )
	)
	~	$/BTU
	~	The lowest equipment cost per unit of energy service (electricity \
		equivalent) among fuels that are actually eligible for this industry and \
		process (nonzero effective shareweight - calibrated or feasibility \
		floored). Used as the reference cost in the relative-cost logit in \
		Industrial Equipment Fuel Choice Weight: each fuel's weight depends on its \
		cost RATIO to this reference, so the cheapest eligible fuel always has \
		weight near shareweight * 10000 and the share denominator cannot fall \
		below Vensim's ZIDZ tolerance (about 1e-6), which previously zeroed every \
		fuel share silently and made new equipment consume no energy at all. \
		Ineligible fuels (zero shareweight, often with zero cost) are pushed out \
		of the minimum by adding 1 dollar per BTU, several orders of magnitude \
		above any real fuel or equipment cost per BTU.
	|

Minimum Share of New Clinker Capacity by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway]=
	0,	{dry kiln with precalciner}
	0,	{dry kiln with CCS}
	0,	{electric kiln}
	0,	{electric kiln with CCS}
	0	{alternative chemistry cement}
	~	Dmnl [0,1,0.01]
	~	Policy lever (cement pathway mandate): the minimum share of each year's \
		new clinker capacity that must be built on each production pathway, at \
		full implementation. Mandated shares are taken first and the cost-driven \
		(logit) shares fill the remainder, so a mandate acts as a floor; a pathway \
		can be mandated before its shareweight (CPSW) opens, which is how \
		procurement pledges and new-line standards pull first-of-a-kind plants \
		forward. If the mandated shares sum to more than one they are scaled to \
		one. Represents China's benchmark rule for new lines, the EU low-carbon \
		public-procurement share, the First Movers Coalition 10 percent pledge and \
		state near-zero procurement. Rides the indst cement pathway mandate \
		implementation schedule. Added 2026-10-12.
	|

Minimum Share of New Clinker Capacity by Pathway This Year[Cement Production Pathway]\
		=
	Minimum Share of New Clinker Capacity by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway]
	* VECTOR ELM MAP(
	    Selected Policy Implementation Schedule[indst cement pathway mandate X dry kiln with precalciner\
		],
	    (Cement Production Pathway-1)
	  )
	~	Dmnl
	~	The cement pathway mandate as implemented this year, on the indst cement \
		pathway mandate implementation schedule (one element per pathway).
	|

