	   ',',
	   'B2'
	)
	~	years
	~		|

Model Run Clinker Capacity Facing Overhaul Decision by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway\
		]=
	MIN(
	  Last Year Clinker Production Capacity Added During Model Run by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway\
		],
	  Model Run Clinker Capacity Reaching Campaign End by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway\
		]
	)
	~	metric tons/Year
	~	Model-run capacity whose campaign ends this year and that therefore faces \
		the same overhaul-or-replace decision as the preexisting fleet (Q4 \
		decision-curve change, 2026-08-26: previously model-run capacity never \
		entered the decision pool and instead decayed at 1/CPAL per year - new \
		builds never faced decisions, and the decision channel went inert once the \
		CPRS schedule ended). Capped by the surviving model-run stock. Uses the \
		same per-pathway overhaul share as the preexisting pool (the logit \
		compares the same overhaul continuation cost vs new-build cost; documented \
		simplification - the continuation cost carries fleet-typical rather than \
		new-build intensity, slightly understating overhaul attractiveness for \
		BAT-built kilns).
	|

Model Run Clinker Capacity Overhauled by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway]=
	Model Run Clinker Capacity Facing Overhaul Decision by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway\
		]
	* Cement Overhaul Share at Decision[Cement Production Pathway]
	~	metric tons/Year
	~	Model-run capacity that overhauls at its campaign-end decision. Stays in \
		the model-run stock and reenters the decision pool as a distributed curve \
		one mean campaign later; its overhaul capital (CPCaOC overhaul cost) is \
		booked with the preexisting pool's via Total Clinker Capacity Overhauled \
		by Pathway.
	|

Model Run Clinker Capacity Reaching Campaign End by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway\
		]= DELAY3I(
	New Clinker Production Capacity by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway]
	+ Model Run Clinker Capacity Overhauled by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway],
	CPPL Cement Pathway Campaign Length[Cement Production Pathway],
	0)
	~	metric tons/Year
	~	Model-run capacity (new builds plus prior model-run overhauls) arriving at \
		its campaign-end decision, distributed around the mean campaign length \
		CPPL (third-order delay) - the model-run analog of Cement Capacity \
		Reentering Decision Pool by Pathway. No feedback loop: DELAY3 output \
		depends on its internal states, not the same-step input. Standalone \
		because delay functions should not be nested inside other functions (KB \
		gotcha).
	|

Model Run Clinker Capacity Retirements by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway]=
	Model Run Clinker Capacity Facing Overhaul Decision by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway\
		]
	- Model Run Clinker Capacity Overhauled by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway]
	~	metric tons/Year
	~	Model-run capacity that retires at its campaign-end decision instead of \
		overhauling (Q4 decision-curve change, 2026-08-26: replaces the blanket \
		1/CPAL age decay - once model-run capacity faces endogenous campaign-end \
		decisions, a parallel asset-life decay would retire the same capacity \
		twice; kiln life now emerges from overhaul economics for BOTH stocks, the \
		same convention the preexisting fleet has had since Phase 2b). Excluded \
		from production in the decision year and replaced the same year through \
		the new-build pathway logit. CPAL remains the greenfield amortization \
		window in the choice cost's capital-recovery factor.
	|

