New Indst Eqpt Energy Intensity Multiplier due to Changes in Fuel Costs[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process]=
	MAX(0.01, 1 +

	Expected Percent Change in Industrial Fuel Cost per Unit Energy[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel\
		,Industrial Process]
	) ^ EoIEECwEC Elasticity of Industrial Equipment Energy Consumption wrt Energy Cost
	~	Dmnl
	~	Constant-elasticity (power) form, (price ratio)^elasticity, rather than \
		the linear approximation 1 + gap*elasticity.  The two match for small gaps \
		(both give about -1% intensity per +10% expected fuel cost, per Linn \
		2008), but the linear form reaches zero energy use at a gap of +1000% \
		while the power form has diminishing returns and never crosses zero - the \
		correct behavior for large carbon-tax-driven gaps, and the functional form \
		Linn's log-log regression actually estimates.  Symmetric in proportional \
		terms for price falls (subsidies), consistent with Linn finding no \
		rise-fall asymmetry.  The price ratio is the expected (foresight-window, \
		hurdle-discounted) policy cost over its BAU twin; the MAX floors the ratio \
		at 0.01 so a near-total fuel subsidy cannot drive a zero or negative base \
		under the negative exponent (at the floor, new-equipment intensity rises a \
		bounded
	|

New Indst Eqpt Energy Intensity Multiplier due to Efficiency Adjustments[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process]=
	IF THEN ELSE(
	  New Industrial Equipment Energy Intensity Multiplier from Efficiency Stds[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process] < 1,

	  MIN(
	    New Indst Eqpt Energy Intensity Multiplier due to Changes in Fuel Costs[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process],
	    New Industrial Equipment Energy Intensity Multiplier from Efficiency Stds[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process]
	  ),

	  New Indst Eqpt Energy Intensity Multiplier due to Changes in Fuel Costs[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process]
	  * New Industrial Equipment Energy Intensity Multiplier from Efficiency Stds[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process]
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

New Industrial Equipment Capital Cost[Industry Category] :EXCEPT: [cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		]=
	SUM(
	  New Industrial Equipment Potential Energy Use by Fuel Type and Process[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel!,Industrial Process
	!]
	  * Industrial Equipment Capital Cost per Unit Energy Before Clean Heat Subsidy[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel!,Industrial Process!]
	)
	+ SUM(Thermal Battery New Energy Service[Industry Category,industrial heating process\
		!]
	* TBCC Thermal Battery Capital Cost per Unit Annual Energy Served[industrial heating process\
		!]) ~~|
New Industrial Equipment Capital Cost[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239]=
	SUM(
	  New Industrial Equipment Potential Energy Use by Fuel Type and Process[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Industrial Fuel!,Industrial Process
	!]
	  * Industrial Equipment Capital Cost per Unit Energy Before Clean Heat Subsidy[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Industrial Fuel!,Industrial Process!]
	)
	+ SUM(Thermal Battery New Energy Service[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239,industrial heating process\
		!]
	* TBCC Thermal Battery Capital Cost per Unit Annual Energy Served[industrial heating process\
		!])
	+ SUM(
	    New Clinker Production Capacity by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway!]
	    * Cement Pathway Capital Cost per Unit Annual Capacity Including Capture Equipment\
		[Cement Production Pathway!]
	  )
	+ SUM(
	    Total Clinker Capacity Overhauled by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway!]
	    * Cement Overhaul Capital Cost per Unit Annual Capacity after RnD[Cement Production Pathway\
		!]
	  )
	+ Cement Calcined Clay Plant Capital Cost
	~	$
	~	Includes thermal battery equipment purchases (new heat service added times \
		TBCC), which sit outside the Industrial Fuel dimension and so cannot ride \
		the fuel-subscripted SUM. Adding them here lets the entire downstream \
		capex chain (financed and non-financed splits, entity booking, Capital and \
		OM Spending ISIC routing) inherit thermal battery equipment spending with \
		no further edits.
	|

