	New Vehicle Price after Fuel Economy Effects[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology\
		]
	* (1 - RnD Transportation Capital Cost Perc Reduction This Year[Vehicle Technology])
	~	$/vehicle
	~		|

New Vehicle Price after RnD Without Subsidies[Cargo Type,Vehicle Type,Vehicle Technology\
		]=
	New Vehicle Price after RnD[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology]
	+ This Year Battery Subsidy Passed Through to Consumers by Vehicle Type[Cargo Type,Vehicle Type\
		,Vehicle Technology]
	~	$/vehicle
	~		|

New Vehicle Price Including EV Shadow Costs[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology\
		] :EXCEPT:    [LDVs,passenger,battery electric vehicle
]=
	New Vehicle Price[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology] ~~|
New Vehicle Price Including EV Shadow Costs[LDVs,passenger,battery electric vehicle]=
	New Vehicle Price[LDVs,passenger,battery electric vehicle]
	+ Range Anxiety Shadow Cost
	+ Charging Availability Shadow Cost
	+ Consumer Preference Shadow Cost[LDVs,passenger,battery electric vehicle]
	~	$/vehicle
	~		|

New Vehicles[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology]=
	QUANTUM(
	  SUM(New Vehicles by Subregion[Subregion!,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology\
		]),
	  QSfV Quantization Size for Vehicles[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type]
	)
	/ One Year
	~	vehicles/Year
	~	If the model wishes to add fewer than +/- VQS vehicles, this is rounding \
		error, and we dampen it to zero.  If we do not, it can throw off the Fleet \
		Average Fuel Economy if the erroneously introduced vehicle (or negative \
		vehicle) is the only vehicle of its type and technology in the model.
	|

New Vehicles Allocated before ZEV Standards[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology\
		]=
	(
	  TTS Transportation Technology Shareweights[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology\
		]
	  * 
	  exp(
	    New Vehicle Cost per Mile[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology]
	    * Vehicle Allocation Unit Correction
	    * TTLE Transportation Technology Logit Exponents[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type]
	  )
	)
	
	/
	
	(
	  SUM(
	    TTS Transportation Technology Shareweights[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology\
		!]
	    * 
	    exp(
	      New Vehicle Cost per Mile[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology!]
	      * Vehicle Allocation Unit Correction
	      * TTLE Transportation Technology Logit Exponents[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type]
	    )
	  )
	)
	* New Vehicles Demanded[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type]
	~	vehicles
	~	Using "Unmodified Logit" function as described at \
		https://jgcri.github.io/gcam-doc/choice.html
	|

New Vehicles before ZEV Standards by Subregion[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology\
		]=
	New Vehicles Allocated before ZEV Standards[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology\
		]
	* VSbS Vehicle Shares by Subregion[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type]
	~	vehicles
	~		|

New Vehicles by Subregion[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology]=
	New Vehicles by Subregion for Vehicle Types without BAU Qualifying Technologies[Subregion\
		,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology]
	+ New Vehicles by Subregion for Vehicle Types with BAU Qualifying Technologies[Subregion\
		,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology]
	~	vehicles
	~		|

New Vehicles by Subregion for Vehicle Types with BAU Qualifying Technologies[Subregion\
		,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology]=
	IF THEN ELSE(Sum of Shareweights by Vehicle and Cargo Type[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type] \
		= 0,
	
	0,
	
	IF THEN ELSE(
	
	  ZEV Sales Share Without ZEV Standard[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type]
	  > ZEV Standard by Subregion[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type],
	
	
	  New Vehicles before ZEV Standards by Subregion[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology\
		],
	
	
	  New Vehicles before ZEV Standards by Subregion[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology\
		]
	    * Vehicle Technologies Qualifying as ZEVs[Vehicle Type,Vehicle Technology]
	    * ZIDZ(
	        ZEV Standard by Subregion[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type],
	        ZEV Sales Share Without ZEV Standard[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type]
	      )
	  + New Vehicles before ZEV Standards by Subregion[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type\
		,Vehicle Technology]
	    * (1 - Vehicle Technologies Qualifying as ZEVs[Vehicle Type,Vehicle Technology])
	    * ZIDZ(
	        (1 - ZEV Standard by Subregion[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type]),
	        (1 - ZEV Sales Share Without ZEV Standard[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type]\
		)
	      )
	)
	)
	~	vehicles
	~	If the ZEV standard is met naturally, we keep the pre-ZEV standard \
		allocation. Otherwise, we scale up ZEVs sales such that the standard is \
		hit and scale down non-ZEV sales so as to avoid changing the total number \
		of vehicles sold.
	|

New Vehicles by Subregion for Vehicle Types without BAU Qualifying Technologies[Subregion\
		,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology]=
	IF THEN ELSE(Sum of Shareweights by Vehicle and Cargo Type[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type] \
		= 0,
	
	
	IF THEN ELSE(
	  
	  ZEV Sales Share Without ZEV Standard[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type]
	  > ZEV Standard by Subregion[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type],
	
	
	  New Vehicles before ZEV Standards by Subregion[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology\
		],
	
	
	  (New Vehicles before ZEV Standards by Subregion[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,\
		Vehicle Technology]
	  * (1 - ZEV Standard by Subregion[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type]))
	
	  + 
	
	  SUM(New Vehicles before ZEV Standards by Subregion[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type\
		,Vehicle Technology!])
	  * ZEV Standard by Subregion[Subregion,Vehicle Type,Cargo Type]
	  * 
	
	  ((Vehicle Technologies Qualifying as ZEVs[Vehicle Type,Vehicle Technology]
	  * exp(New Vehicle Cost per Mile[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology]* Vehicle Allocation Unit Correction
	  * TTLE Transportation Technology Logit Exponents[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type])
	)
	/
	(
	  SUM(Vehicle Technologies Qualifying as ZEVs[Vehicle Type,Vehicle Technology!]
	  * exp(New Vehicle Cost per Mile[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology!]* Vehicle Allocation Unit Correction
	  * TTLE Transportation Technology Logit Exponents[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type])
	  )
	))
	
	
	)
	
	,0)
	~	vehicles
	~		|

New Vehicles Demanded[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type]=
	INTEGER(
	 ZIDZ(
	  New Vehicle Distance Traveled[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type],
	  Average Annual Dist Traveled by Vehicle Type Weighted by Technology[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type\
		]
	 )
	 +0.999999
	)
	~	vehicles
	~		|

New Vehicles Last Year[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology]= DELAY FIXED (
	New Vehicles[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology],
	1,
	0)
	~	vehicles/Year
	~		|

New Vehicles over Fuel Economy[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology]=
	IF THEN ELSE(New Vehicle Fuel Economy[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology] > \
		0, (New Vehicles[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology]) / New Vehicle Fuel Economy\
		[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology], IF THEN ELSE(Start Year Fleet Avg Fuel Economy\
		[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology] > 0, (New Vehicles[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type\
		,Vehicle Technology]) / Start Year Fleet Avg Fuel Economy[Vehicle Type,Cargo Type,Vehicle Technology\
		], 0))
	~	vehicles/(miles/BTU)/Year
	~		|

New Waste Heat Measure Capital Expenditures[Industry Category]=
	Waste Heat Availability Index[Industry Category]
	* SUM(
	    New Waste Heat Measure Deployment This Year[Industry Category,Waste Heat Measure\
		!,Measure Cost Level!]
	    * MCLS Measure Cost Level Share[Measure Cost Level!]
	    * (WHMFSP Waste Heat Measure Fuel Savings Potential[Industry Category,Waste Heat Measure\
		!]
	       * Industrial Heat Combustion Fuel Base for Measures[Industry Category]
	       + WHMESP Waste Heat Measure Elec Savings Potential[Industry Category,Waste Heat Measure\
		!]
	       * Industrial Heat Electricity Base for Measures[Industry Category])
	    * WHMCC Waste Heat Measure Capital Cost per Unit Annual Energy Saved[Industry Category\
		,Waste Heat Measure!]
	  )
	~	$
	~	Capital cost of waste heat measure savings capacity newly deployed this \
		year, priced against the current-year energy base at unadjusted input \
		costs.
	|

New Waste Heat Measure Deployment This Year[Industry Category,Waste Heat Measure,Measure Cost Level\
		]=
	IF THEN ELSE(
	  WHMFSP Waste Heat Measure Fuel Savings Potential[Industry Category,Waste Heat Measure\
		]
	  + WHMESP Waste Heat Measure Elec Savings Potential[Industry Category,Waste Heat Measure\
		] <= 0,
	
	  0,
	
	  MIN(
	    MAX(
	      0,
	      MIN(
	        Waste Heat Measure Potential Remaining After BAU Deployment[Industry Category\
		,Waste Heat Measure],
	      MAX(
	        Waste Heat Measure Tranche Economically Deployable[Industry Category,Waste Heat Measure\
		,Measure Cost Level
	],
	        Min Fraction of Waste Heat Measure Potential Deployed This Year[Industry Category\
		]
	      ))
	      - MAX(
	          0,
	          Last Year Deployed Fraction of Waste Heat Measure Potential[Industry Category\
		,Waste Heat Measure,Measure Cost Level
	]
	          - Waste Heat Measure Deployment Retired This Year[Industry Category,Waste Heat Measure\
		,Measure Cost Level]
	        )
	    ),

	    Waste Heat Measure Deployment Retired This Year[Industry Category,Waste Heat Measure\
		,Measure Cost Level]
	    + MAX(
	        SoCEMDSiaY Share of Cost Effective Measure Deployment Started in a Year
	        * MAX(
	            0,
	            MIN(
	              Waste Heat Measure Tranche Economically Deployable[Industry Category,Waste Heat Measure\
		,Measure Cost Level],
	              Waste Heat Measure Potential Remaining After BAU Deployment[Industry Category\
		,Waste Heat Measure]
	            )
	            - Last Year Deployed Fraction of Waste Heat Measure Potential[Industry Category\
		,Waste Heat Measure,Measure Cost Level]
	          ),

	        MAX(
	          0,
	          MIN(
	            Min Fraction of Waste Heat Measure Potential Deployed This Year[Industry Category\
		],
	            Waste Heat Measure Potential Remaining After BAU Deployment[Industry Category\
		,Waste Heat Measure]
	          )
	          - Last Year Deployed Fraction of Waste Heat Measure Potential[Industry Category\
		,Waste Heat Measure,Measure Cost Level]
	        )
	      )
	  )
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Deployment this year, as a fraction of tranche potential.  Retiring \
		capacity is replaced in full (replacing worn-out equipment that is still \
		cost effective is routine maintenance, not a fresh adoption decision, so \
		it is not held back by the annual start-rate).  Genuinely new deployment \
		is rate limited: the economic channel starts SoCEMDSiaY of the remaining \
		gap to its ceiling each year, while a binding standard deploys \
		immediately.  The outer MIN caps the level at whichever target is higher, \
		so a tranche that stops being cost effective decays by retirement instead \
		of being replaced.  Both channels are capped at the potential remaining \
		after BAU-case deployment (no cap in the US, where that share is zero).
	|

Newly Overhauled Preexisting Clinker Capacity by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway]=
	Preexisting Clinker Capacity Overhauled by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway]
	* (1 - Overhauled Share of Preexisting Clinker Capacity by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway\
		])
	~	metric tons/Year
	~	Start-year capacity overhauled this year for the first time: this year's \
		overhauls less the part that, pro rata, had already been overhauled once \
		(a second overhaul does not add to the overhauled stock).
	|

Newly Persistently Deep Unviable for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source]=
	Boolean Persistently Deep Unviable for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source]
	* (1 - Last Year Boolean Persistently Deep Unviable for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source\
		])
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

NGPS industry fuel within all fuels:
	natural gas,
	petroleum gasoline,
	petroleum diesel,
	jet fuel or kerosene,
	crude oil,
	heavy or residual fuel oil,
	LPG propane or butane
	~	
	~		|

