Perc Subsidy for Cement Pathway Capital Cost[Cement Production Pathway]=
	0,	{dry kiln with precalciner}
	0,	{dry kiln with CCS}
	0,	{electric kiln}
	0,	{electric kiln with CCS}
	0	{alternative chemistry cement}
	~	Dmnl [0,1,0.01]
	~	Policy lever (cement pathway capital subsidy): the fraction of the \
		greenfield capital cost of new clinker capacity on each production pathway \
		(kiln plus any capture equipment) that government pays, at full \
		implementation, on top of any BAU subsidy (BCPCS; the two together are \
		capped at the whole cost). It lowers the capital term in the pathway \
		choice (Cement Pathway Levelized Cost per Ton of Clinker) and is paid out \
		through Cement Pathway Investment Subsidy Amount Paid; the capital booking \
		itself stays gross, as for the clean industrial heat and thermal battery \
		investment subsidies. Represents capital grants and investment tax credits \
		for low-carbon cement plants (EU Innovation Fund grants of roughly 20-40 \
		percent of project cost, Canada's 50 percent capture-equipment credit, the \
		cancelled US DOE demonstration awards at 25-50 percent). Rides the indst \
		cement pathway capital subsidy implementation schedule. Added 2026-10-12.
	|

Perc Subsidy for Cement Pathway Capital Cost This Year[Cement Production Pathway]=
	Perc Subsidy for Cement Pathway Capital Cost[Cement Production Pathway]
	* VECTOR ELM MAP(
	    Selected Policy Implementation Schedule[indst cement pathway capital subsidy X dry kiln with precalciner\
		],
	    (Cement Production Pathway-1)
	  )
	~	Dmnl
	~	The cement pathway capital subsidy as implemented this year, on the indst \
		cement pathway capital subsidy implementation schedule (one element per \
		pathway).
	|

