Percent Reduction in Cement Content of Concrete=
	0
	~	Dmnl [0,0.2,0.01]
	~	Policy lever (cement content): fraction by which the binder content per \
		cubic meter of concrete is reduced at constant concrete demand and \
		performance through mix optimization - admixtures, aggregate gradation, \
		mix design quality control, longer cure times. It does not include \
		replacing cement with SCMs, which belongs to the clinker-substitution \
		lever (Fraction of Cement Measures Achieved), so the two levers do not \
		overlap; their effects multiply (less cement per cubic meter, less clinker \
		per ton of cement). Distinct also from material efficiency, which reduces \
		concrete volume. Literature supports roughly 10-20% technical potential; \
		rides the indst cement measures implementation schedule. Economics: booked \
		as a cement-targeted material-efficiency entry, injected into the Material \
		Efficiency Improvement matrix's ISIC 239 source row (scaled by CSoIO to \
		239-product terms), so the buyer's avoided cement purchase, 239's lost \
		revenue, the buyer price index, and the passthrough all book through the \
		standard machinery. The physical cut is carried cement-only at full \
		strength by Total Cement Demand's (1 - lever) factor and divided back out \
		of the production-percent fold-in (see Cement Content Lever Component of \
		239 Output Change). The unit-cost capex normalization stays on pre-lever \
		demand.
	|

Percent Reduction in Cement Content of Concrete This Year=
	Percent Reduction in Cement Content of Concrete
	* Selected Policy Implementation Schedule[indst cement measures X]
	~	Dmnl
	~	The cement-content lever as implemented this year, on the same schedule as \
		the other cement measures.
	|

