Process Emissions after CCS[Industry Category,Pollutant]=
	Process Emissions before CCS[Industry Category,Pollutant]
	- This Year Process Pollutants Sequestered by Industry Sector[Industry Category,Pollutant\
		]
	~	g pollutant
	~		|

Process Emissions before CCS[Industry Category,Pollutant] :EXCEPT:  [agriculture and forestry 01T03\
		,CO2], [cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239,CO2]=
	MAX((BAU Process Emissions before CCS[Industry Category,Pollutant]
	     + SUM(Decrease in Process Emissions at BAU Production Levels[Industry Category,\
		Industry Process Emissions Policy!,Pollutant
	])
	     + SUM(Non BAU Process Emissions Additions at BAU Production Levels[Industry Category\
		,Industry Process Emissions Policy!,Pollutant])
	     + Change in Process Emissions from Feedstock Shifting[Industry Category,Pollutant\
		]
	    )
	    * (1 + Percent Change in Production due to Policies[Industry Category])
	  ,0
	  ) ~~|
Process Emissions before CCS[agriculture and forestry 01T03,CO2]=
	(
	  BAU Process Emissions before CCS[agriculture and forestry 01T03,CO2]
	  + SUM(Decrease in Process Emissions at BAU Production Levels[agriculture and forestry 01T03\
		,Industry Process Emissions Policy!,CO2])
	  + SUM(Non BAU Process Emissions Additions at BAU Production Levels[agriculture and forestry 01T03\
		,Industry Process Emissions Policy!,CO2])
	  + Change in Process Emissions from Feedstock Shifting[agriculture and forestry 01T03\
		,CO2]
	)
	* (1 + Percent Change in Production due to Policies[agriculture and forestry 01T03])\
		 ~~|
Process Emissions before CCS[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239,CO2]=
	MAX(
	  (
	    BAU Cement Residual Process CO2
	    + SUM(Decrease in Process Emissions at BAU Production Levels[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Industry Process Emissions Policy!,CO2])
	    + SUM(Non BAU Process Emissions Additions at BAU Production Levels[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,Industry Process Emissions Policy!,CO2])
	    + Change in Process Emissions from Feedstock Shifting[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,CO2]
	  )
	  * (1 + Percent Change in Production due to Policies[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		])
	  ,0
	)
	+ Cement Process CO2 Emissions
	~	g pollutant
	~	The cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239 CO2 branch: the generic \
		process-emissions machinery (MAC-curve decreases/additions, feedstock \
		shifting, production scaling) acts on the non-cement RESIDUAL only, and \
		the cement module's endogenous process CO2 - which already carries the \
		policy production change through its own demand chain - is added on top. \
		NOTE: the inert indst cement measures MAC element currently targets the \
		residual (lime etc.) here; if that lever is ever activated it belongs \
		INSIDE the module (the planned SCM/clinker-substitution lever), not in \
		this branch. SYNC NOTE: the residual part duplicates the generic branch's \
		form - mirror edits.
	|

