Reduction Achieved by Marginal Cost[Industry by Process Emissions Policy,Marginal Abatement Cost\
		] :EXCEPT: [cement industry measures,Marginal Abatement Cost]=
	Reduction Achieved by Marginal Cost Excluding Carbon Tax Driven Reductions[Industry by Process Emissions Policy\
		,Marginal Abatement Cost]
	+ Process Emissions Abated due to Carbon Tax by Marginal Cost[Industry by Process Emissions Policy\
		,Marginal Abatement Cost] ~~|
Reduction Achieved by Marginal Cost[cement industry measures,Marginal Abatement Cost]\
		=
	0
	{RETIRED WITH THE CEMENT BREAKOUT (levers block, 2026-08-26): the
	Process Emissions Policies lever for cement measures is repurposed as
	the clinker-substitution (SCM) lever - Fraction of Cement Measures
	Achieved now drives Fraction of Additional Clinker Substitution This
	Year in the cement pathway module, which reduces clinker demand (and
	hence calcination CO2 and kiln fuel) mechanistically rather than
	through this MAC allocation. Left un-retired, setting the lever would
	fire the MAC machinery against the non-cement RESIDUAL of 239's
	process emissions (lime and other carbonates) AND double-count with
	the module response. The retirement lives HERE, one node below the
	ALLOCATE AVAILABLE, because Vensim rejects an EXCEPT split on the
	ALLOCATE equation itself (batch LOADMODEL parse failure, verified
	2026-08-26). Companion retirement: the carbon-tax branch of Process
	Emissions Abated due to Carbon Tax by Marginal Cost (Phase 2a).}
	~	g CO2e
	~		|

Reduction Achieved by Marginal Cost Excluding Carbon Tax Driven Reductions[Industry by Process Emissions Policy\
		,Marginal Abatement Cost]=
	ALLOCATE AVAILABLE(
	  Remaining Avoidable Process Emissions after Carbon Tax[Industry by Process Emissions Policy\
		,Marginal Abatement Cost],
	  Process Emissions Cost Parameters as Vector[Marginal Abatement Cost,ptype],
	  Increase in Process CO2e by Policy and Industry[Industry by Process Emissions Policy\
		]
	)
	~	g CO2e
	~		|

