Share of Low Carbon Cement Premium Paid by Government=
	1
	~	Dmnl [0,1,0.05]
	~	Share of the low-carbon cement premium that government pays (1 for public \
		Buy Clean procurement, 0 for a private advance market commitment). The \
		government share is a cash flow to the cement industry; the private share \
		is a transfer between cement buyers and makers inside the nonenergy \
		industries and is not booked separately. Policy design setting entered in \
		Vensim.
	|

Share of Max Hourly Exports Met[Electricity Timeslice,Hour,Optimization Pass]=
	ZIDZ(Electricity Exports by Hour[Electricity Timeslice,Hour,Optimization Pass],
	  MaMHEIaE Maximum Hourly Exports)
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Share of Max Hourly Imports Met[Electricity Timeslice,Hour,Optimization Pass]=
	ZIDZ(Electricity Imports by Hour[Electricity Timeslice,Hour,Optimization Pass],
	  Effective Maximum Hourly Electricity Imports[Electricity Timeslice,Hour])
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Share of Maximum Annual Decrease in Demand from Diurnal Grid Batteries=
	ZIDZ(
	  Maximum Annual Decrease in Demand from Diurnal Grid Batteries,
	
	  (Maximum Annual Decrease in Demand from Diurnal Grid Batteries
	  + Maximum Annual Decrease in Demand from EVs
	  + Maximum Annual Decrease in Demand from Pumped Hydro
	  + Maximum Annual Decrease in Demand from Seasonal Electricity Storage
	  )
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Share of New Clinker Production Capacity by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway]=
	Mandated Share of New Clinker Capacity by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway]
	+ Required Low Carbon Share of New Clinker Capacity * Low Carbon Pathway Allocation of Required New Clinker Capacity\
		[Cement Production Pathway]
	+ (1 - SUM(Mandated Share of New Clinker Capacity by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway\
		!]) - Required Low Carbon Share of New Clinker Capacity)
	  * Cost Driven Share of New Clinker Production Capacity by Pathway[Cement Production Pathway\
		]
	~	Dmnl
	~	Pathway shares of this year's new clinker capacity: the mandated shares \
		first, then the required low-carbon capacity split among the low-carbon \
		pathways, then the cost-driven logit shares scaled to fill the rest. The \
		shares always sum to one; with no mandate or requirement this is the logit \
		share.
	|

Share of New Industrial Equipment Allocated by Fuel Type in Electricity Equivalent[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process] :EXCEPT: [Industry Category,Industrial Fuel,industrial heating process\
		]=
	ZIDZ(
	  Industrial Equipment Fuel Choice Weight[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process\
		],
	  SUM(Industrial Equipment Fuel Choice Weight[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel!,Industrial Process\
		])
	) ~~|
Share of New Industrial Equipment Allocated by Fuel Type in Electricity Equivalent[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,industrial heating process]=
	TBEM Thermal Battery Eligibility Mask[industrial heating process]
	* ZIDZ(
	  Industrial Equipment Fuel Choice Weight[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel,industrial heating process\
		],
	  SUM(Industrial Equipment Fuel Choice Weight[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel!,industrial heating process\
		])
	  + Thermal Battery Choice Weight[Industry Category,industrial heating process]
	)
	+ (1 - TBEM Thermal Battery Eligibility Mask[industrial heating process])
	* ZIDZ(
	  Industrial Equipment Fuel Choice Weight[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel,industrial heating process\
		],
	  SUM(Industrial Equipment Fuel Choice Weight[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel!,industrial heating process\
		])
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Using standard "Logit" function as described at \
		https://jgcri.github.io/gcam-doc/choice.html. The heating branch is a \
		segmented market: for the TBEM-eligible fraction of buyers, fuels compete \
		against thermal batteries (thirteen-way denominator); for the remaining \
		1-TBEM fraction, thermal batteries are not an option and the plain \
		twelve-fuel logit applies. Fuel shares plus Thermal Battery Share of New \
		Industrial Equipment (TBEM times the thirteen-way battery share) still sum \
		to exactly one. TBEM enters here rather than as a choice-weight multiplier \
		because a weight multiplier cannot cap the share when the battery weight \
		dominates the logit. With TBS at zero the heating branch reduces exactly \
		to the twelve-fuel logit.
	|

Share of New Industrial Equipment by Fuel Type and Process in Electricity Equivalent[\
		Industry Category,Target Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process]=
	Share of New Industrial Equipment by Fuel Type and Process in Electricity Equivalent after Electrification Policy\
		[Industry Category
	,Target Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process]
	*
	(1 - Fraction of Eligible Industrial Energy Use Shifted to Alternate Fuel This Year[\
		Industry Category,Industrial Process])
	
	+ 
	
	SUM(
	  Share of New Industrial Equipment by Fuel Type and Process in Electricity Equivalent after Electrification Policy\
		[Industry Category,Source Industrial Fuel!,Industrial Process]
	  * NIEAFSM New Industrial Equipment Alternative Fuel Shifting Matrix[Target Industrial Fuel\
		,Source Industrial Fuel!]
	)
	* Fraction of Eligible Industrial Energy Use Shifted to Alternate Fuel This Year[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Process]
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Share of New Industrial Equipment by Fuel Type and Process in Electricity Equivalent after Electrification Policy\
		[Industry Category
,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process] :EXCEPT:    [Industry Category,electricity if,Industrial Process\
		]=
	Share of New Industrial Equipment Allocated by Fuel Type in Electricity Equivalent[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process]
	- Share of New Industrial Equipment Allocated by Fuel Type in Electricity Equivalent\
		[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process]
	* IFStE Industrial Fuels Subject to Electrification[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel\
		]
	* Fraction of Eligible Industrial Energy Use Shifted to Electricity This Year[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Process] ~~|
Share of New Industrial Equipment by Fuel Type and Process in Electricity Equivalent after Electrification Policy\
		[Industry Category
,electricity if,Industrial Process]=
	Share of New Industrial Equipment Allocated by Fuel Type in Electricity Equivalent[Industry Category\
		,electricity if,Industrial Process]
	
	+ SUM(
	    Share of New Industrial Equipment Allocated by Fuel Type in Electricity Equivalent\
		[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel!,Industrial Process]
	    * IFStE Industrial Fuels Subject to Electrification[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel\
		!]
	  )
	  * Fraction of Eligible Industrial Energy Use Shifted to Electricity This Year[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Process]
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Share of New Industrial Equipment by Fuel Type in Electricity Equivalent[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel]=
	ZIDZ(
	  SUM(Output from New Industrial Equipment by Fuel Type and Industrial Process[Industry Category\
		,Industrial Fuel,Industrial Process
	!]),
	
	  SUM(Output from New Industrial Equipment[Industry Category,Industrial Process!])
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Share of New Passenger LDV EV Purchases Requiring Home Charger Installations=
	(1-Last Year Percent Vehicle Stock by Vehicle Technology[LDVs, passenger,battery electric vehicle\
		])
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Share of Off Grid Electricity Demand That is New This Year Met by Power Plant Type[Electricity Source\
		]=
	ZIDZ(
	
	  (
	    GHESS Green Hydrogen Electricity Supply Shareweights[Electricity Source]
	    * exp(MAX(1, Cost per Unit New Elec Output Using Expected Capacity Factors[Electricity Source\
		]/Cost per Unit New Elec Output Unit Correction Factor
	)/10^4*GHESLE Green Hydrogen Electricity Supply Logit Exponent
	  )
	  ),
	
	  (
	    SUM(GHESS Green Hydrogen Electricity Supply Shareweights[Electricity Source!]
	    * exp(MAX(1, Cost per Unit New Elec Output Using Expected Capacity Factors[Electricity Source\
		!]/Cost per Unit New Elec Output Unit Correction Factor
	)/10^4*GHESLE Green Hydrogen Electricity Supply Logit Exponent
	  )
	  )
	)
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~	Allocation of new dedicated off-grid capacity across power plant types, \
		shared by BOTH consumers of dedicated off-grid electricity: green hydrogen \
		electrolysis and industrial thermal battery charging (consolidated \
		2026-08-17 - a separate thermal battery copy with identical TBESS \
		shareweights previously existed and was mathematically identical). GHESS \
		restricts the eligible sources (onshore wind and solar PV by default). If \
		procurement mixes ever need to differ by use (electrolyzers favor high \
		capacity factor, battery charging is diurnal), re-split this variable per \
		use.
	|

Share of Output by Energy Supplier Cash Flow Entity[Cash Flow Entity]=
	ZIDZ(
	  SUM(BAU Output by ISIC Code by Year[Fossil and Energy Utility ISIC Code!]),
	
	  SUM(BAU Output by ISIC Code by Year[ISIC Code!])
	)
	* Share of Fuel Production by Energy Supplier Cash Flow Entity[Cash Flow Entity]
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Share of Output that is Fuel Costs by Industry Category[Industry Category ]=
	ZIDZ(SUM(Amount Spent on Industry Fuels[Industry Category,Industrial Fuel!]),
	        Output by ISIC Code by Year[Industry Category ISIC Code])
	~	Dmnl
	~		~	:SUPPLEMENTARY 
	|

Share of Preexisting Buildings Subject to Retrofitting[Building Type]=
	0,	{urban residential}
	0,	{rural residential}
	0,	{commercial}
	0	{data centers}
	~	Dmnl [0,1]
	~		|

Share of Preexisting Buildings Subject to Retrofitting To Date[Building Type]=
	Share of Preexisting Buildings Subject to Retrofitting[Building Type]
