		] ~~|
This Year Energy Related Pollutants Sequestered by Industry Sector[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,CO2]=
	MAX(
	  0,
	  SUM(Industrial Sector Energy Related Emissions before CCS[Industrial Fuel!,cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,CO2])
	  - Cement Kiln Combustion CO2 Emissions
	)
	* Fraction of CO2 Captured by Industry Category[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,energy related emissions]
	+ Cement Combustion CO2 Captured by Pathway Capture
	~	g pollutant
	~	Energy-related pollutants captured and sequestered by each industry this \
		year: energy-related CO2 times the industry's capture fraction. For \
		industry 239 the generic fraction applies only to fuel CO2 outside the \
		cement module's kilns, and the module's own CCS-pathway capture of \
		kiln-fuel CO2 is added as tons, matching the process-emissions treatment.
	|

This Year Financing Repayments for Cement Pathway Equipment=
	Last Year Financing Repayments for Cement Pathway Equipment
	+ Annual Financing Repayment for Newly Purchased Cement Pathway Equipment
	- Annual Cement Pathway Equipment Financing Repayments Expiring After Repayment Period
	~	$
	~	Repayments due this year on financed cement pathway capital (new builds \
		plus kiln overhauls): last year's active obligations plus this year's new \
		loans, less the streams that reach the end of the repayment period. Same \
		setup as This Year Financing Repayments for Industrial CCS Equipment.
	|

This Year Financing Repayments for Cement Pathway Equipment at Unsubsidized Rate=
	Last Year Financing Repayments for Cement Pathway Equipment at Unsubsidized Rate
	+ Annual Financing Repayment for Newly Purchased Cement Pathway Equipment at Unsubsidized Rate
	- Annual Cement Pathway Equipment Financing Repayments at Unsubsidized Rate Expiring After Repayment Period
	~	$
	~	Counterfactual-rate twin of This Year Financing Repayments for Cement \
		Pathway Equipment (loans priced at the unsubsidized annuity factor), for \
		the financing-instrument cost accounting.
	|

