		] :EXCEPT: [Industry Category,CO2]=
	0 ~~|
This Year Process Pollutants Sequestered by Industry Sector[Industry Category,CO2] :EXCEPT:\
		 [cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239,CO2]=
	Process Emissions before CCS[Industry Category,CO2]
	* Fraction of CO2 Captured by Industry Category[Industry Category,process emissions]\
		 ~~|
This Year Process Pollutants Sequestered by Industry Sector[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,CO2]=
	(Process Emissions before CCS[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239,CO2]
	 - Cement Process CO2 Emissions)
	* Fraction of CO2 Captured by Industry Category[cement and other nonmetallic minerals 239\
		,process emissions]
	+ Cement Process CO2 Captured by Pathway Capture
	~	g pollutant
	~	Industry 239's sequestered process CO2: the generic retrofit fraction \
		applies to the non-cement residual (lime and other minerals) only, and the \
		cement module's own CCS-pathway capture is added as tons (2026-10-01 \
		reconciliation). Everything downstream - transport and storage, subsidies, \
		O&M, capture energy, the process-emissions netting - then treats cement \
		capture like any other industrial capture, booked once.
	|

This Year Solar and Wind Hard Costs as Fraction of Last Year Hard Costs[Electricity Source\
		] :EXCEPT:    [solar PV es],[onshore wind es
],[offshore wind es]=
	0 ~~|
This Year Solar and Wind Hard Costs as Fraction of Last Year Hard Costs[onshore wind es\
		]=
	(1 - PDiCCpDoC Perc Decline in Capacity Cost per Doubling of Capacity[onshore wind es\
		])
	^ MAX(0, LN(
	        This Year Cumulative Electricity Generation Capacity Affecting Learning[onshore wind es\
		]
	        / Last Year Cumulative Electricity Generation Capacity Affecting Learning[onshore wind es\
		]
	      )
	    / LN(2)
	  ) ~~|
This Year Solar and Wind Hard Costs as Fraction of Last Year Hard Costs[solar PV es]=
	(1 - PDiCCpDoC Perc Decline in Capacity Cost per Doubling of Capacity[solar PV es])
	^ MAX(0, LN(
	        This Year Cumulative Electricity Generation Capacity Affecting Learning[solar PV es\
		]
	        / Last Year Cumulative Electricity Generation Capacity Affecting Learning[solar PV es\
		]
	      )
	    / LN(2)
	  ) ~~|
This Year Solar and Wind Hard Costs as Fraction of Last Year Hard Costs[offshore wind es\
		]=
	(1 - PDiCCpDoC Perc Decline in Capacity Cost per Doubling of Capacity[offshore wind es\
		])
	^ MAX(0, LN(
	        This Year Cumulative Electricity Generation Capacity Affecting Learning[offshore wind es\
		]
	        / Last Year Cumulative Electricity Generation Capacity Affecting Learning[offshore wind es\
		]
	      )
	    / LN(2)
	  )
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

This Year Total Grid Battery Storage Capacity excluding Hybrid Batteries=
	This Year Grid Battery Storage Capacity excluding Hybrid Batteries
	+ This Year Cumulative Policy Mandated Grid Battery Storage
	~	MW*hour
	~		|

This Year Total Grid Battery Storage Capacity excluding Hybrid Batteries in MW=
	This Year Total Grid Battery Storage Capacity excluding Hybrid Batteries
	/ GBSC Diurnal Grid Battery Daily Storage Duration
	~	MW
	~		|

This Year Vintage Flag[Vintage]=
	IF THEN ELSE(
	  Vintage to Year Mapping[Vintage] = Dimensionless Time,
	
	  1,
	
	  0
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Three Year Average CF Scaling Revenue for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source]=
	IF THEN ELSE(Time = INITIAL TIME,
	  CF Scaling Revenue per Unit Capacity for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source\
		],
	  IF THEN ELSE(Time = INITIAL TIME + 1,
	    (CF Scaling Revenue per Unit Capacity for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source\
		]
	     + Last Year CF Scaling Revenue per Unit Capacity for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source\
		]) / 2,
	    (CF Scaling Revenue per Unit Capacity for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source\
		]
	     + Last Year CF Scaling Revenue per Unit Capacity for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source\
		]
	     + Two Years Prior CF Scaling Revenue per Unit Capacity for Cost Driven Retirement\
		[Electricity Source]) / 3))
	~	$/MW
	~		|

Three Year Average Fleet Generation Hours for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source\
		]=
	IF THEN ELSE(Time = INITIAL TIME,
	  Fleet Average Generation Hours for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source],
	  IF THEN ELSE(Time = INITIAL TIME + 1,
	    (Fleet Average Generation Hours for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source]
	     + Last Year Fleet Average Generation Hours for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source\
		]) / 2,
	    (Fleet Average Generation Hours for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source]
	     + Last Year Fleet Average Generation Hours for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source\
		]
	     + Two Years Prior Fleet Average Generation Hours for Cost Driven Retirement[Electricity Source\
		]) / 3))
	~	hours
	~		|

Three Year Average Net Energy Market Revenue by Plant Type Excluding Subsidies for Hybrid Power Plants\
		[Hybrid Electricity Source]=
	DEPRECIATE STRAIGHTLINE(
	 One Year Average Net Energy Market Revenue by Plant Type Excluding Subsidies for Hybrid Power Plants\
		[Hybrid Electricity Source],
	 3,
	 1,
	 0
	)
	~	$/MW
	~		|

Three Year Average Total Predicted Net Energy Market Revenue per MW[Electricity Source\
		]=
	DEPRECIATE STRAIGHTLINE(
	 Last Year Five Year Average Annual Net Revenue per MW by Power Plant Type[Electricity Source\
		],
	 3,
	 1,
	 0
	)
	~	$/(MW*hr)
	~		|

Three Year Average Wholesale Energy Market Costs=
	DEPRECIATE STRAIGHTLINE(
	 One Year Average Wholesale Energy Market Costs,
	 3,
	 1,
	 0
	)
	~	$
	~		|

Three Year Weighted Average Hypothetical Electricity Capacity Factor[Electricity Timeslice\
		,Hour,Electricity Source]=
	(Last Year Hypothetical Hourly Electricity Capacity Factor[Electricity Timeslice,Hour\
		,Electricity Source]
	+ Two Years Prior Hypothetical Hourly Electricity Capacity Factor[Electricity Timeslice\
		,Hour,Electricity Source]
	+ Three Years Prior Hypothetical Hourly Electricity Capacity Factor[Electricity Timeslice\
		,Hour,Electricity Source]
	)
	/3
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Three Years Prior Hypothetical Hourly Electricity Capacity Factor[Electricity Timeslice\
		,Hour,Electricity Source]= DELAY FIXED (
	  Two Years Prior Hypothetical Hourly Electricity Capacity Factor[Electricity Timeslice\
		,Hour,Electricity Source],
	  1,
	  SYSHECF Start Year Seasonal Expected Hourly Electricity Capacity Factors[Electricity Source\
		,Electricity Timeslice,Hour
	] * RAF Regional Availability Factor for Generation[Electricity Source])
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

TIOT Minus A Matrix[Source ISIC Code, Target ISIC Code]=
	Identity Matrix for ISIC Codes[Source ISIC Code, Target ISIC Code]
	- Total Input Output Table after Material Efficiency[Source ISIC Code, Target ISIC Code\
		]
	~	Dmnl
	~	I minus A for the total (domestic plus imported) technical coefficients, \
		including the material efficiency reduction, so the total Leontief inverse \
		stays consistent with the domestic one.
	|

TIOT Total Input Output Table[Source ISIC Code,Target ISIC Code]=
	GET DIRECT CONSTANTS(
	   'InputData/io-model/TIOT/TIOT.csv',
	   ',',
	   'B2'
	)
	~	Dmnl
	~		|

Toggle Carbon Tax Border Adjustment=
	0
