12,316,0,-31,2524,211,32,8,135,0,4,-1,0,0,0,-1--1--1,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
If production would exceed production cap and there is room under the import cap, shift some production to imports.  Vice versa if imports would exceed import cap.
12,317,0,618,2613,400,28,8,135,0,4,-1,0,0,0,-1--1--1,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
If both the production and import caps are exceeded, we allocate the excess change in fuel use to production and imports, exceeding both caps proportionately to the cap sizes.
12,318,0,-407,2521,108,36,8,135,0,4,-1,0,0,0,-1--1--1,255-255-128,|||0-0-0,0,0,0,0,0,0
We apportion change in fuel use into change in production and change in imports by the relative importance of these two modes.
